# T2: TIMED arm B of the paired ABAB on coding prompts, eight users live (audits off): A = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-time-gate (the control: the same eight 262k seats and the nine levers,
# one SDPA launch per user per layer), B = c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-sdpamulti (the same profile plus QWEN_FAST_TP4_SDPA=multi: ONE launch per layer per 64-row block, one G16 entry per user, 16 cores per entry, flags 0x21). The flag is the
# ONLY difference (test_sdpa_multi_tp holds it). Arms alternate A B A B in this one image, each after its own all-four reset.
# The tests: warmup, one coding stream, concurrent8_steady (the smoke rule of the eight-seat quad blocks), eight 32k code users and eight about 120,000-token users (concurrent8_code_128k, 800 out), eight live at once.
# READ: the [PACKED-PHASE] round times of the eight-user tests, PAIRED per round, never by unpaired medians (check the load average around the run: a busy host skews a timed phase 10 to 20%, so
# no build, no CI push and no other job beside it), the per-seat rate = committed tokens per round per user / round time, and the texts equal between the arms. Then offline: python scripts/ci/speed_window_compare.py
# <A results> <B results> --users 0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7 --position-keyed --strict-concurrent-prefixes (exit 0 identical). THE PREDICTION (design K2, estimated, never measured): about -6 ms per 64-row block at 4k mean context, about -18 ms at 48k and
# about -42 ms at 131k, so about -12 / -36 / -84 ms per eight-seat round; a multi round no faster than the control is the finding (the one-launch cost of a dominant user, 3 row tiles on 16 cores, or the in-trace gather).
# Duration (estimate): 90 min. Soft.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/sdpa-multi eight-seat 262k development window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/sdpa-multi and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a
# registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from this branch by its author.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sdpa-multi-1 is what B0 builds from the pushed tp4/sdpa-multi commit; every later job serves that one image. A commit of a
# file the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-sdpa-multi-2
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-best-sdpamulti
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k
